%%   ③ Lambda alphaforge-intake and ④ Lambda alphaforge-context (+ explainer templates in S3) exist, but the
%%     deployed API runs both IN-PROCESS (AF_INTAKE_MODE=bedrock, AF_CONTEXT_MODE unset = local).
%%   ① frontend: static S3 + CloudFront (deploy_frontend.py; --api-url routes /v1/* to the Function URL) ·
%%     Cognito user pool + web client + 3 shared demo accounts (setup_cognito.py).
%% BUILT IN CODE: ⑤ orchestration = Strands GRAPH by default (AF_ORCHESTRATION=graph): the plan's sub-agents run
%%   as parallel fork nodes, an AND-join feeds one synthesis node (Claude Sonnet, holds governance_check);
%%   AF_ORCHESTRATION=tools = the older agents-as-tools orchestrator (serial) · 6 sub-agents (Claude Haiku) ·
%%   governance_check = deterministic tool (rules.yaml) · evidence hook → ledger (DynamoDB, or JSONL in data/runs
%%   locally) · Explainer (Claude Sonnet, structured sections, deterministic claim check, retry once then remove,
%%   honest fallback) · optimizer tool (cvxpy, allocation sub-agent) · profile from a PDF / Word file (onboarding) ·
%%   notification settings (SMS / email) and account deletion · AgentCore entrypoint (app/entrypoint.py).
%% DIVERGES from target: ⑤ runs inside the API Lambda, not AgentCore Runtime (entrypoint ready, not deployed) ·
%%   no API Gateway: Function URL + in-app JWT verification · uploads go through the API (5 MB, never stored),
%%   not S3 presigned URLs · Memory (L17): with AF_MEMORY_ID the long-term soft preferences reach the synthesis
%%   prompt, but in graph mode (the default) the short-term session manager is not attached to any agent.
%% NOT BUILT: Guardrails grounding check on the answer (L18) · AgentCore Observability wiring · S3 offload of
%%   large run results (DynamoDB 400 KB item limit).
