flowchart TB
  %% ===== 1. Frontend =====
  %% AWS: S3 + CloudFront (static HTML/CSS/JS, no server) · Cognito (login → JWT) · S3 presigned URLs (uploads).
  %%      Plain web app instead of Streamlit: full control of design tokens, light/dark modes, focus and
  %%      control states (Hallmark rules, Bastien & Scapin criteria). Locally: served by the API (StaticFiles).
  %%      On AWS: scripts/deploy_frontend.py → private S3 bucket read by CloudFront only (Origin Access Control),
  %%      managed security headers; with --api-url, CloudFront also routes /v1/* to the API Gateway (same origin:
  %%      no CORS, the Cognito Bearer token is forwarded). config.js = the Cognito settings from setup_cognito.py.
  UI["① Frontend — web app (HTML/CSS/JS) on S3 + CloudFront · Cognito login<br/>my portfolio (built from the profile) · ask (chat) · profile set-up chat (questions or a PDF / Word file) · profile form · analysis plan · settings (alerts, account)"]

  %% ===== 2. API =====
  %% AWS: Lambda (container image from ECR, built by CodeBuild) + Function URL · FastAPI + Mangum.
  %%      Target: API Gateway HTTP API + Cognito JWT authorizer (not used: the API verifies tokens itself).
  API["② API — Lambda Function URL (FastAPI, container image)<br/>POST /v1/runs → 202 run_id (or 200 question) · GET /v1/runs[/id, /evidence, /catalog, /replay]<br/>GET/PUT /v1/profile · POST /v1/profile/draft[/file] · GET/PUT /v1/notifications · DELETE /v1/account · GET /v1/me"]

  %% ===== 3. Intake =====
  %% AWS: Bedrock (Claude Haiku, Converse API + structured outputs JSON Schema) · Guardrails (input)
  subgraph INTAKE["③ Intake — Bedrock Haiku, structured output (Pydantic)"]
    ING["Intake agent (ingester)<br/>free text → validated JSON"]
    PROF[/"Profile JSON<br/>risk band · horizon · ESG / crypto prefs<br/>language · experience · agent toggles"/]
    REQ[/"Request JSON<br/>task · assets · weights · capital · as_of"/]
  end

  %% ===== 4. Context =====
  %% AWS: Lambda (plain Python code) · S3 or Bedrock Prompt Management (versioned templates)
  subgraph CTX["④ Context resolution — deterministic code, no LLM"]
    PLAN{{"Plan resolver<br/>task × profile × toggles → enabled sub-agents"}}
    LOAD{{"Prompt loader<br/>Explainer prompt by experience level × wants to learn<br/>(versioned explainer.level[.learning].md templates in S3)"}}
  end

  %% ===== 5. Agents =====
  %% AWS: Bedrock (Sonnet, Haiku) · AgentCore Memory. CURRENT host: the API Lambda (asynchronous self-invocation).
  %%      Target host: Bedrock AgentCore Runtime (app/entrypoint.py is ready, not deployed).
  subgraph RT["⑤ Agents — Strands graph (runs in the API Lambda · target: AgentCore Runtime)"]
    ORCH["Orchestrator / synthesis node<br/>Claude Sonnet"]
    MEM[("AgentCore Memory<br/>session · soft preferences")]
    subgraph SUB["Sub-agents · Claude Haiku · enabled by the plan · parallel graph fork nodes"]
      RISK["Risk"]
      NEWS["News"]
      ESG["ESG"]
      FUND["Fundamentals"]
      MACRO["Macro & scenarios"]
      ALLOC["Allocation<br/>(self-verifies via GOV)"]
    end
    GOV["Governance check — deterministic<br/>rules.yaml → PASS / WARN / BLOCK"]
    EXP["Explainer agent · Claude Sonnet<br/>cites evidence only + deterministic claim check (retry once, then remove)"]
  end

  %% ===== 6. Tools & data =====
  %% AWS: AgentCore Gateway (MCP) · Lambda · Neptune Serverless · Bedrock Knowledge Bases · S3 Vectors · S3 · DynamoDB
  subgraph DATA["⑥ Tools & data"]
    GW["AgentCore Gateway (MCP) → quant tools Lambda<br/>metrics · concentration · correlation · risk_contribution<br/>macro_snapshot · fx_usdcad · market screen / related · esg_screen<br/>(in-process: rate_sensitivity · company_fundamentals · optimize · governance_check)"]
    NEP[("Neptune Serverless market graph<br/>31 core assets + S&P 500 · ESG · holdings · correlations<br/>refreshed 11:00 / 17:00 ET")]
    KB["Bedrock Knowledge Base<br/>news & docs · S3 Vectors"]
    S3[("S3 curated Parquet<br/>prices · FX · macro · point-in-time")]
    DDB[("DynamoDB<br/>profiles · runs · evidence ledger · alert contacts")]
  end

  %% ===== News alerts (side process, no LLM) =====
  %% AWS: Lambda alphaforge-news-alerts · EventBridge Scheduler (every 15 min, 7:00-22:45 Toronto) · SNS (SMS).
  %%      Opted-in contacts × the tickers of their saved portfolio → new SEC 8-K filings → one fixed-wording text.
  ALR["News alerts — deterministic Lambda<br/>EventBridge every 15 min · SEC filings → SNS SMS"]

  %% AWS: same static frontend (S3 + CloudFront); reads the result via API Gateway + Lambda
  OUT["⑦ Frontend result view + portfolio dashboard<br/>short answer · clickable evidence · checks · trace · charts by detail level"]

  %% ===== Cross-cutting =====
  %% AWS: Bedrock Guardrails · AgentCore Observability → CloudWatch (GenAI observability) · IAM
  X["Cross-cutting: Bedrock Guardrails (inputs & outputs) · AgentCore Observability → CloudWatch · IAM least privilege"]

  %% ===== Flow =====
  %% L1  UI → API: Cognito issues the JWT (ID token, sent as Bearer). TARGET: an API Gateway JWT authorizer
  %%      validates it before the Lambda. CURRENT (deployed): CloudFront routes /v1/* to the Lambda Function URL
  %%      (auth NONE) and the API verifies the token itself (AF_AUTH_MODE=cognito, see below).
  %%      Demo accounts share one password, published in config.js on purpose (one-click demo).
  %%      BUILT: user pool alphaforge-users + public web client alphaforge-web (scripts/setup_cognito.py): email +
  %%      password, sign-up with an emailed code, forgot password, 3 demo accounts (amira/mateo/robert.demo@
  %%      alphaforge.example) whose profile is seeded from personas.json on first sign-in. The browser calls Cognito
  %%      directly (USER_PASSWORD_AUTH, refresh); the API sends the ID token as Bearer. Without API Gateway
  %%      (locally and on the Function URL), AF_AUTH_MODE=cognito makes the API verify it itself
  %%      (backend/app/api/auth.py: JWKS, RS256, iss, aud, exp, token_use=id).
  %%      Files (profile from a PDF / Word document) go through the API: multipart upload, 5 MB cap, text extracted
  %%      and never stored. Target: S3 presigned URLs for larger files.
  UI -->|"JWT"| API
  %% L2  API → Intake: the API Lambda (backend/app/api/, FastAPI + Mangum) runs the Intake and the context
  %%      resolution synchronously (a few s, under API Gateway's 30 s): it answers 200 with the Intake's
  %%      question or "create your profile first", else saves the run QUEUED and answers 202 {run_id}.
  %%      With AF_INTAKE_MODE=lambda and AF_CONTEXT_MODE=lambda the API invokes two separate Lambdas:
  %%      alphaforge-intake does only the model step ({"op": "extract"}: Guardrails + Haiku → IntakeDraft) and the
  %%      API keeps the merge with the stored profile, the toggles and the storage; alphaforge-context returns the
  %%      ExecutionPlan + PromptRef. CURRENT (deployed API): both run IN-PROCESS (deploy_api.py sets
  %%      AF_INTAKE_MODE=bedrock and no AF_CONTEXT_MODE), which is also the local and test default.
  %%      Identity = Cognito JWT `sub` (X-Actor-Id header only with AF_AUTH_MODE=dev).
  %%      The Intake calls Bedrock (Haiku) with structured outputs (JSON schema), via the anthropic
  %%      SDK (AnthropicBedrock client = InvokeModel, messages.parse, inference profile us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5);
  %%      code: backend/app/intake/. Guardrails filters the input (prompt attack, personal data): ApplyGuardrail
  %%      when AF_GUARDRAIL_ID is set. Offline mode without an LLM (AF_INTAKE_MODE=mock) for tests and demos.
  API --> ING
  %% L3  Intake → JSON: output validated by schema (Bedrock structured outputs), then Pydantic;
  %%      the profile is stored in DynamoDB (ACTOR#… / PROFILE#current), including the sub-agent toggles the user
  %%      switches on/off in chat (with their words: agent_toggle_reasons) and the profile form (PUT /v1/profile).
  %%      Onboarding: POST /v1/profile/draft[/file] reads the person's answers or a PDF / Word file (text extracted by
  %%      the API, never stored) with the intake model and returns the fields found, what is missing and what was
  %%      irrelevant; nothing is saved until the person saves (PUT /v1/profile). Code: app/intake/onboarding.py.
  %%      The profile also keeps the user's current portfolio (portfolio + portfolio_run_id: the mix AlphaForge built
  %%      from it, saved by the web app); a question about "my portfolio" naming no asset gets its positions from it.
  ING --> PROF
  ING --> REQ
  %% L4  JSON → Plan resolver: plain Python code; versioned agent/task registry
  %%      (backend/app/core/plan_registry.yaml, or AWS AppConfig as an option). Output: ExecutionPlan.
  PROF --> PLAN
  REQ --> PLAN
  %% L5  Profile → Prompt loader: Lambda alphaforge-context (see L2); picks the Explainer template from experience × wants_to_learn
  %%      (5 templates: beginner/intermediate get a ".learning" variant with a glossary; advanced has one).
  %%      wants_to_learn comes from the profile form or from what the user says ("I'm a student"), never from
  %%      age or other demographics. Source: Git (backend/app/prompts/explainer.<level>[.learning].md),
  %%      published to S3 by scripts/deploy_context_lambda.py (AF_PROMPT_SOURCE=s3); option: Bedrock Prompt
  %%      Management. Output: PromptRef (level, style, version, sha256).
  PROF --> LOAD
  %% L6  Plan → Orchestrator: TARGET: DynamoDB (run QUEUED) → "dispatcher" Lambda → AgentCore Runtime
  %%      (InvokeAgentRuntime). CURRENT (AF_DISPATCH=lambda, deployed): POST /v1/runs saves the run QUEUED, answers
  %%      202 and invokes the SAME Lambda asynchronously ({"af_dispatch_run": run_id}); that invocation runs the
  %%      orchestrator then the Explainer and writes RUNNING → DONE / FAILED. Async retries are off (0), so a
  %%      run is never analysed twice; a run cut by the 15-min Lambda timeout stays RUNNING (not swept yet).
  %%      Locally: AF_DISPATCH=inline (default, before POST returns) | local (background thread) | none.
  PLAN -->|"ExecutionPlan"| ORCH
  %% L7  Prompt loader → Explainer: only keys travel (level, style, version, sha256) in the run record; the
  %%      Explainer loads the template and refuses it if its version or sha256 changed since planning.
  LOAD -.->|"prompts"| EXP
  %% L8  Orchestrator → Sub-agents: CURRENT default (AF_ORCHESTRATION=graph, app/agents/graph.py): a Strands
  %%      GraphBuilder with one fork node per plan-enabled sub-agent (run in worker threads, in parallel) and an
  %%      AND-join into the synthesis node (Sonnet); each fork's envelope is appended to the run ledger.
  %%      AF_ORCHESTRATION=tools: agents-as-tools — ORCH calls each <domain>_subagent tool in turn. Either way the
  %%      payload is structured (subject + weights + tickers) and the investor context is rendered into the brief by
  %%      deterministic code (render_brief). Target: the same graph hosted in AgentCore Runtime.
  ORCH -->|"dispatch (parallel graph)"| SUB
  %% L9  Governance: governance_check is a deterministic TOOL (pure-Python rules over rules.yaml, no LLM):
  %%      the synthesis node (graph mode) or ORCH (tools mode) calls it on the weights for the reference verdict,
  %%      and ALLOC self-verifies its proposal by iterating until PASS/WARN — L10's "BLOCK → fix" loop.
  %%      Checks: single position and sector (equity ETFs decomposed), crypto, horizon rules, exclusions
  %%      (asset class, ESG activity, verified controversies), ESG index preference. No loss-limit rule yet.
  ORCH -->|"governance_check (tool)"| GOV
  ALLOC -->|"self-verify loop"| GOV
  %% L10 Governance → caller: the verdict returns to whoever called the tool (synthesis / ORCH or ALLOC);
  %%      max 2 loops implemented inside ALLOC's iterate-to-PASS.
  GOV -->|"verdict (PASS / WARN / BLOCK)"| ORCH
  %% L11 Governance → Explainer: the top-level governance verdicts (orchestrator or synthesis, from the ledger) +
  %%      the plan's disabled agents; each written check must match its verdict's evidence, else the verdict is shown as is.
  GOV -->|"PASS / WARN"| EXP
  %% L12 Sub-agents → Tools: AF_GATEWAY_URL set (deployed): the quant tools go through the AgentCore Gateway (MCP,
  %%      SigV4; one MCPClient per URL, shared) to the quant tools Lambda (metrics, concentration, correlation,
  %%      risk_contribution, macro_snapshot, fx_usdcad, market screen / related, esg_screen). Unset: the same
  %%      functions run in-process (app/tools/toolsets.py). Always in-process: rate_sensitivity,
  %%      company_fundamentals (SEC XBRL, point-in-time), news_search, optimize (cvxpy), governance_check.
  %%      Toolsets per sub-agent: risk: metrics/concentration/correlation/risk_contribution + market_screen/
  %%      market_related · macro: macro_snapshot/rate_sensitivity/correlation · esg: esg_screen ·
  %%      fundamentals: company_fundamentals + news_search(8-K) + esg_screen · allocation: optimize/metrics/
  %%      concentration/governance_check + market_screen/market_related (candidate discovery; optimize still gates
  %%      tickers on the dated returns). Target option: Cedar policies at the Gateway (AgentCore Policy).
  SUB -->|"tool calls (MCP / in-process)"| GW
  %% L13 News → KB: Bedrock Knowledge Base "alphaforge-news-docs" (Titan Text Embeddings v2, S3 Vectors index, metadata
  %%      filter published_date <= as_of applied BEFORE ranking), deployed by scripts/deploy_news_kb.py (AF_KB_ID).
  %%      Corpus: news_index.csv (SEC 8-K filings with the text of the reported item, rate decisions; no press headlines)
  %%      and the annual-report risk / legal sections. Without AF_KB_ID the sub-agent falls back to news_search, a
  %%      keyword search over the same file with the same date rule; SIMULATED (labeled fictional) only if that file is
  %%      missing. After scripts/ingest_news.py or scripts/enrich_8k.py, re-run deploy_news_kb.py to re-sync and re-index.
  NEWS -.->|"RAG · published ≤ as_of"| KB
  %% L14 Tools → Data: the quant tools Lambda reads the curated Parquet on S3 (AF_CURATED_S3, written by
  %%      scripts/deploy_data_layer.py; pandas + fastparquet, point-in-time as-of filter). In-process tools read the
  %%      same tables through app/tools/curated_store.py (S3 Parquet or the repo CSVs; the API image bakes data/ in).
  GW --> S3
  GW -->|"screen · related · esg (freshness-gated)"| NEP
  %% Market graph (app.market): LIVE Neptune snapshot (or the identical LocalGraph over data/market
  %%      Parquet), refreshed 11:00/17:00 ET business days. Reliable within AF_GRAPH_FRESH_HOURS (12h
  %%      default) of Snapshot.loaded_at/intraday_at; a STALE graph refuses every graph tool
  %%      (market_screen/market_related/esg_screen) instead of serving outdated data. Price series stay
  %%      in Parquet: metrics/correlation/optimize remain point-in-time over the curated store.
  %%      LOCAL fast path (app/tools/market_store.py): the same S3 market tables synced into
  %%      data/market (manifest included, so the 12h rule stays honest) serve market_screen/
  %%      market_related/esg_screen from the in-process LocalGraph — milliseconds, no gateway hop,
  %%      no Lambda cold start; the Gateway path (AF_GATEWAY_URL) stays the deployed route. One
  %%      MCPClient per gateway URL is shared across sub-agents and runs (warm handshake).
  %%      WARM-UP at intake: run_intake / the dispatcher kick off a daemon thread
  %%      (market_store.kick_off_market_warmup) that syncs the cache and probes the quant Lambda
  %%      once, so Neptune's wake (~9s idle) happens during the intake LLM call, not during the
  %%      forks. The quant Lambda runs an always-warm "live" alias with provisioned concurrency 1
  %%      (memory 1769MB) behind the Gateway targets; sub-agent prompts batch independent tool
  %%      calls into one turn (they execute concurrently).
  %% L15 Tools → Evidence ledger: a Strands hook (Before/AfterToolCallEvent) fires around every
  %%      tool call. Sink: DynamoDB (RUN#<id> / EVID#<seq>#<evidence_id>, atomic EVIDSEQ counter for the parallel
  %%      forks) when AF_STORE=dynamodb (deployed API); locally the JSONL ledger data/runs/<run_id>.jsonl behind
  %%      the same EvidenceLedger interface — every call is
  %%      one record (seq, caller agent tag, tool, inputs, envelope, wall-time duration_ms),
  %%      incl. nested sub-agent calls and failures; graph fork nodes also record their
  %%      execution_time as duration_ms. Viewer: scripts/show_run.py (ms column + per-caller totals).
  GW -->|"each call = 1 evidence"| DDB
  %% L16 DynamoDB → Explainer: reads the run's ledger (EvidenceLedger.records) and builds an evidence catalogue
  %%      (every evidence_id, nested ones linked to their parent); the claim check compares each stated
  %%      number with the evidence it cites. Same catalogue served by GET /v1/runs/{id}/evidence/catalog.
  DDB -.->|"evidence ledger"| EXP
  %% L17 Orchestrator ↔ Memory: AgentCore Memory, on the main agent only (sub-agents stay stateless).
  %%      Short term: the conversation, stored per (actorId, sessionId) by the Strands session manager and restored
  %%      on the next turn (the API returns session_id). Long term: userPreferenceMemoryStrategy extracts SOFT
  %%      preferences into /preferences/{actorId}/; code loads them at each run into the system prompt.
  %%      They guide tone and emphasis, never override profile or governance, and are not evidence.
  %%      Setup: scripts/agentcore_memory.py create --write-env (AF_MEMORY_ID). Without it the run goes on, memory off.
  %%      GAP: in graph mode (the default) only the long-term preferences are used (synthesis prompt); the session
  %%      manager is built but attached to no agent, so the short-term conversation is not kept. Tools mode keeps both.
  ORCH <-.-> MEM
  %% L18 Explainer → DynamoDB: RunRecord.result["answer"] (RunAnswer: sections, citations, verification,
  %%      model, PromptRef) via the RunStore. Target: S3 if > 400 KB; Guardrails grounding check (not built).
  EXP -->|"RunResult"| DDB
  %% L19 Explainer → Result view: in practice the frontend polls GET /v1/runs/{id} (API Gateway + Lambda
  %%      that reads DynamoDB). Option: API Gateway REST with response streaming (SSE) for progress.
  EXP -->|"GET /v1/runs/id (poll)"| OUT
  %% Alerts: the news-alert Lambda reads the opted-in contacts and their saved portfolios from DynamoDB, fetches
  %%      the new SEC filings on those tickers, and texts one fixed-wording message (no model, never advice) via SNS.
  %%      Dedupe per filing (SMSSENT log). Not yet: phone ownership check (OTP) beyond the SNS sandbox, and the
  %%      "at most one text a day" promise shown in the settings is not enforced by the code.
  DDB -.->|"contacts · saved portfolios"| ALR

  classDef aws fill:#fff4e5,stroke:#e88a1a,color:#1f1f1f;
  classDef det fill:#eaf2ff,stroke:#3b6fd8,color:#1f1f1f;
  classDef agent fill:#eaf8ee,stroke:#2f9e55,color:#1f1f1f;
  classDef json fill:#f6f0ff,stroke:#8a63d2,color:#1f1f1f;
  classDef ui fill:#ffffff,stroke:#555,color:#1f1f1f;
  class API,GW,KB,S3,DDB,MEM,NEP,X aws;
  class PLAN,LOAD,GOV,ALR det;
  class ING,ORCH,RISK,NEWS,ESG,FUND,MACRO,ALLOC,EXP agent;
  class PROF,REQ json;
  class UI,OUT ui;

%% =====================================================================================
%% GLOSSARY OF AWS TOOLS (summary)
%% -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%% Amazon CloudFront: CDN in front of the S3 bucket holding the frontend's static files (HTTPS, caching).
%% (ECS on Fargate + ALB were planned for a Streamlit frontend; not needed for a static web app.)
%% Amazon Cognito: user directory; issues the JWT tokens (pseudonymous identity = actor_id).
%% Amazon S3: object storage. Uploaded files (presigned URLs), curated Parquet, prompt templates.
%% Amazon API Gateway (HTTP API): managed HTTPS entry point; validates the JWT; times out at 30 s
%%   (hence the asynchronous runs). REST APIs offer response streaming up to 15 min.
%% AWS Lambda: on-demand code (15 min max). FastAPI API + agents (container image), quant tools, market refresh /
%%   graph loader, news alerts. Function URL: a Lambda's own HTTPS endpoint (used instead of API Gateway).
%% Amazon ECR + AWS CodeBuild: image registry and the managed build that produces the API image (no local Docker).
%% Amazon Neptune Serverless: managed graph database (openCypher) holding the market graph, inside a VPC.
%% Amazon EventBridge Scheduler: cron schedules (market refresh 11:00 / 17:00 ET, news alerts every 15 min).
%% Amazon SNS: sends the news-alert text messages (SMS sandbox: verified numbers only).
%% Amazon Bedrock: API access to models (Claude Sonnet / Haiku, Titan Embeddings).
%%   Structured outputs: response that conforms to a JSON schema (replaces forced toolChoice).
%% Bedrock Prompt Management (option): versioned prompts with variables, deployed by version.
%% Bedrock AgentCore Runtime: hosts the agents (managed container, one isolated session per analysis).
%% Strands Agents (AWS open-source library, not a service): agents, tools, graph, hooks.
%% AgentCore Memory: short-term (session) and long-term (preferences) memory per user.
%% AgentCore Gateway: exposes Lambdas / APIs as shared MCP tools, with authentication.
%% AgentCore Policy (option): Cedar rules evaluated at the Gateway to allow / deny a tool.
%% Bedrock Knowledge Bases: managed RAG (ingestion, chunking, embeddings, search with filters).
%% Amazon S3 Vectors: low-cost vector storage and search in S3; KB index.
%% Amazon DynamoDB: serverless key-value NoSQL database. Profiles, runs, events, evidence.
%% Bedrock Guardrails: configurable filters (denied topics, prompt attack, personal data,
%%   contextual grounding) on model inputs and outputs.
%% AgentCore Observability: OpenTelemetry traces from the agents to CloudWatch (GenAI observability view).
%% Amazon CloudWatch: logs, metrics, dashboards, alarms.
%% AWS IAM: roles and permissions; one least-privilege role per component.
%% Not used: AWS CDK (infrastructure is created by the boto3 scripts in scripts/deploy_*.py) · Secrets Manager ·
%%   Step Functions · Glue + Athena (SQL on S3).
%% =====================================================================================
